  "title": "Gustar",
  "sortOrder": 14,
  "prerequisiteId": "plurals",
  "explanation": "Gustar works backwards from the English verb to like. The thing is the subject. Me gusta el café means the coffee is pleasing to me. A plural thing uses gustan: me gustan los libros.\n\nThe little word matches the person: me, te, le, nos, os, les. Os is the Spain form for a group you know.",
  "commonMistake": "Saying yo gusto el café. The usual sentence is me gusta el café.",
